  "translations": {
    "Linh Ung is a complete pagoda visit on its own; any forest-road viewpoint is a separate, access-dependent add-on.": "靈應寺本身就是完整的參訪行程；森林道路上的觀景點則是另一段行程，須視通行狀況而定。",
    "My Khe stands on its own as a public shore visit; An Thuong is a separate neighborhood stop after the midday break.": "美溪海灘適合獨立安排為公共海岸行程；安順區是午間休息後另訪的街區。",
    "Set above Da Nang Bay, Linh Ung is a Buddhist complex with a sequence of spaces, not simply its prominent Lady Buddha statue. Da Nang’s tourism portal describes its design as bringing modern and traditional Vietnamese pagoda architecture together in the three-door gate, main hall and ancestral house. Visitors pass the gate into a courtyard of bonsai and arhat figures, then see Buddhist images and sculptural reliefs of Shakyamuni’s life inside the hall. The principal statue is locally called Lady Buddha; the city portal identifies it as a Lady Bodhisattva and notes the ocean and coastal views along the approach. Local accounts connect the statue with protection for fishermen facing storms and strong waves, giving the sea-facing visit meaning beyond its panorama. Son Tra’s coastal forest is also habitat for the endangered red-shanked douc langur, so a sighting is a chance encounter rather than a promised part of a temple visit.": "峴港灣上方的靈應寺是一座由多個空間串連而成的佛教寺院建築群，不只是醒目的觀音像。峴港觀光網站說明，其設計融合越南現代與傳統寺院建築風格，體現在三門、正殿與祖堂。遊客穿過三門，進入有盆景與羅漢像的庭院，再到正殿欣賞佛像及描繪釋迦牟尼一生的浮雕。主要供奉的觀音像在當地稱為 Lady Buddha；市府觀光網站稱其為 Lady Bodhisattva，並提到沿途可眺望海洋與海岸。當地傳說觀音像能庇佑漁民渡過風暴與大浪，因此面海參訪的意義不只有遠眺風景。山茶半島的海岸森林也是瀕危紅腿白臀葉猴的棲地；野生動物只能視為偶然相遇，並非寺院行程中保證能看到的內容。",
    "Son Tra routes can close or be restricted. Before adding an upper road, check the city’s current visitor notice, stay on authorized roads and obey barriers.": "加入上方道路前，先查看市府最新遊客公告，僅行駛獲准道路並遵守路障管制。"
  }
